:"PTGFR","gene_symbol_current":"PTGFR","gene_id":"ENSG00000122420","nucleus_tested":false,"nucleus_significant":null,"nucleus_direction":"not tested","nucleus_padj":null,"nucleus_log2fc":null,"nucleus_score":null,"pct_ad":null,"pct_control":null,"donor_test":"not significant","donor_padj":0.941708,"donor_log2fc":-0.0316335,"donor_lfcse":0.126923,"donor_log2fc_shrunk":-0.001737,"degas_log2fc":null,"degas_padj":null},{"cell_type":"In","gene_symbol":"PTGFR","gene_symbol_current":"PTGFR","gene_id":"ENSG00000122420","nucleus_tested":false,"nucleus_significant":null,"nucleus_direction":"not tested","nucleus_padj":null,"nucleus_log2fc":null,"nucleus_score":null,"pct_ad":null,"pct_control":null,"donor_test":"not significant","donor_padj":0.699807,"donor_log2fc":-0.196977,"donor_lfcse":0.104854,"donor_log2fc_shrunk":-0.010826,"degas_log2fc":null,"degas_padj":null}],"modules":[{"cell_type":"In","gene_id":"ENSG00000122420","module":"blue","kme":0.24797,"hub":false,"module_direction":"lower in AD","module_padj":0.137528,"module_significant":false}],"degas_bulk_de":false,"drug_target":false}},"description":[{"gene_id":"ENSG00000122420","entrez_id":["5737"],"uniprot":["P43088"],"ncbi_summary":"The protein encoded by this gene is member of the G-protein coupled receptor family. This protein is a receptor for prostaglandin F2-alpha (PGF2-alpha), which is known to be a potent luteolytic agent, and may also be involved in modulating intraocular pressure and smooth muscle contraction in uterus. Knockout studies in mice suggest that the interaction of PGF2-alpha with this receptor may initiate parturition in ovarian luteal cells and thus induce luteolysis. Two transcript variants encoding different isoforms have been found for this gene. [provided by RefSeq, Jul 2008].","ncbi_source":"NCBI Gene summary (RefSeq), via MyGene.info","uniprot_function":[{"accession":"P43088","text":"Receptor for prostaglandin F2-alpha (PGF2-alpha). The activity of this receptor is mediated by G proteins which activate a phosphatidylinositol-calcium second messenger system. Initiates luteolysis in the corpus luteum (By similarity). Isoforms 2 to 7 do not bind PGF2-alpha but are proposed to modulate signaling by participating in variant receptor complexes; heterodimers between isoform 1 and isoform 5 are proposed to be a receptor for prostamides including the synthetic analog bimatoprost."}],"uniprot_source":"UniProtKB/Swiss-Prot Function, release 2026_04","retrieved":"2026-10-21"}],"structures":[],"alphafold_accessions":[]}